SHADOW EVALUATOR ROOT CAUSE FIX
================================
File: tools/shadow-evaluator/src/index.ts

ROOT PROBLEM:
  Line ~line 240 (in main()):
    await fs.writeFile('shadow-results/divergence-count.txt', report.divergenceCount.toString());
  
  This OVERWRITES on every run. When batches 2 and 3 ran clean (0 divergences),
  they wiped the evidence from batch 1 (20 divergences).

FIX — REPLACE THE WRITE with an APPEND + RECONCILE pattern:

BEFORE:
  await fs.writeFile('shadow-results/divergence-count.txt', report.divergenceCount.toString());

AFTER:
  // NEVER overwrite — append run metadata, let reconcile-audit.ts derive the count
  const runMeta = JSON.stringify({
    runId: `run-${Date.now()}`,
    mode: report.mode,
    totalEvaluated: report.totalEvaluated,
    divergenceCount: report.divergenceCount,
    ranAt: Date.now(),
  }) + '\n';
  await fs.appendFile('shadow-results/run-manifest.jsonl', runMeta);
  
  // divergence-count.txt is now READ-ONLY for CI/CD tooling
  // Only scripts/ops/reconcile-audit.ts is authoritative
  console.log('[SHADOW] Run metadata appended to run-manifest.jsonl');
  console.log('[SHADOW] Do NOT read divergence-count.txt in CI. Use reconcile-audit.ts');

ALSO FIX in passive-mirror liveEvaluator():
  Current mock always returns { allowed: true } 
  This is why batches 2 and 3 had zero divergences — 
  the live outcome was also mocked as true, creating artificial agreement.
  
  The liveEvaluator must call the ACTUAL executeSlash dry-run path,
  or accept the real live outcome as input (it already does via evaluateIncident params).
  The mock is the bug — remove it.
